[?2004l[?2004h> # MLService Deployment Fix
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Problem
[?2004l[?2004h> Service failed with "No module named 'tokenizers'" even though:
[?2004l[?2004h> - tokenizers was in requirements.txt
[?2004l[?2004h> - pip install -r requirements.txt exited successfully
[?2004l[?2004h> - `python -c "import tokenizers"` worked fine
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Root Causes
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. **Shell alias override**: `~/.bashrc` contained `alias python='/usr/bin/python3'` which forced all `python` commands to use the system Python instead of the virtual environment Python, even when the venv was activated.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. **Wrong working directory**: The service must be run from `/home/user` (parent directory), not from `/home/user/mlservice`, because Python's `-m` flag needs to find the `mlservice` package in the Python path.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Solution
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Fixed Issues:
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. Commented out the problematic alias in `~/.bashrc`:
[?2004l[?2004h>    ```bash
[?2004l[?2004h>    #alias python='/usr/bin/python3'
[?2004l[?2004h>    ```
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. Created `start.sh` launcher script that:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Changes to the correct working directory (`/home/user`)
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Activates the virtual environment
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Runs the service with the venv's Python
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Production Deployment
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> **Use the launcher script:**
[?2004l[?2004h> ```bash
[?2004l[?2004h> /home/user/mlservice/start.sh
[?2004l[?2004h> ```
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> **Or manually:**
[?2004l[?2004h> ```bash
[?2004l[?2004h> cd /home/user
[?2004l[?2004h> source mlservice/.venv/bin/activate
[?2004l[?2004h> python -m mlservice
[?2004l[?2004h> ```
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> **Important:** Always run from `/home/user`, NOT from `/home/user/mlservice`!
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Why It Seemed to Work Sometimes
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> The `python -c "import tokenizers"` test passed because:
[?2004l[?2004h> - It was using the system Python (due to the alias)
[?2004l[?2004h> - The system Python happened to have tokenizers installed globally
[?2004l[?2004h> - But the service needed the venv's packages, which weren't accessible through the aliased Python
